  "measures": [],
  "notes": "Four beams from one 1064 nm laser, 0.5 W each, focused to 50 µm from four sides onto one point: two crossed standing waves. Polarised out of the bench plane (s), all four interfere, a checkerboard of intensity (cos kx + cos kz)² sixteen times one beam’s. Select the screen in the middle and open its Trap tab: for ⁸⁷Rb each site is a trap about 0.3 mK deep with frequencies near 160 kHz both ways in the plane (and about 1 kHz out of it, where only the beams’ widths hold it). Zoom right in on the middle (below 50 µm across) to see the lattice itself. Set the four sources to p (in the plane) and the two standing waves no longer interfere with each other: half the depth, each direction trapped only by its own pair. Lengthen one arm by a fraction of a wavelength (move a source a few hundred nm) and the pattern shifts, as an unlocked lattice drifts in the lab.",
